@* Load-bearing, despite looking like boilerplate — the same note as samples/LegacyHost.

   A project with no .razor files at all is not treated as a Blazor project by the Razor SDK, so
   the Blazor framework static web assets — _framework/blazor.server.js among them — are never
   contributed to it. The page then renders, MapBlazorHub answers on /_blazor/negotiate, and the
   component still never appears: the browser 404s on the script, so the circuit never starts.
   For this host that failure is worse than useless, because a page with no component on it has
   no overflow and no covered tablist, and every geometry assertion passes. *@

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor
